🐛 Describe the bug
I found that the following code will have the risk of memory cross-border access on the ROCM platform:
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/master/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/Embedding.cu#L102
int match_found_this_thread =
         (dst_row == indices_batch[chunk_start - batch_start + threadIdx.x]);
if(threadIdx.x >= n_this_chunk)
          match_found_this_thread = 0;

I think the following code is more secure:
int match_found_this_thread = 0;
if(threadIdx.x < n_this_chunk)
          match_found_this_thread = (dst_row == indices_batch[chunk_start - batch_start + threadIdx.x]);

root cause of this issue:
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/master/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/Embedding.cu#L282
indices_batch_shm_size = 64 * 16 * sizeof(int) :
sizeof(accscalar_t)*warp_size*BLOCKDIMY + sizeof(int)*warp_size*BLOCKDIMY,

if n = 1024 on the  ROCM , the last loop is :
 indices_batch[1008 + threadIdx.x]); // threadIdx = 0 ~ 63,  indices_batch[1008 + 63] may be accessed , but shm size is 1024 

Versions
code branch :  v1.11.
cc @jeffdaily @sunway513 @jithunnair-amd @ROCmSupport @KyleCZH @VitalyFedyunin @jamesr66a

🐛 Describe the bug
The IOS benchmark tutorial  from official website does not work.
https://pytorch.org/tutorials/recipes/mobile_perf.html#benchmarking
↓ tutorial begin

↑  tutorial end
After solving some packages dependence,  after a long time of compiling I reach the stage of  compile success and setup.rb the xcode project, unfortunately, the xcode project seem  not to be  real benchmark project, there is no benchmark code  found inside. The AppDelegate.mm is empty.
the android benchmark code speed_benchmark_torch.cc is not ported.
This really waste a lot of time!  hope to see a real official IOS benchmark!
